      "features": "<p >Verified: Windows x64, Unity 6000.0.83f1, Built-in Render Pipeline, Entities 1.3.15. Install required Unity packages through Package Manager. Other platforms and render pipelines have not been validated.</p></br><p >Automatic discovery supports compatible opaque MeshRenderer/MeshFilter pairs with one submesh/material and positive uniform hierarchy scale. Unsupported rendering remains unchanged with an explanation. Serialized prefab references are supported; Resources, Addressables and AssetBundle loading require dedicated integration.</p></br><p >Includes nine interface languages, offline documentation and three optional samples. Editor analysis is a preview; conversion is applied in player builds.</p>",
      "optional": "<p >Entity Forge helps projects that use many copies of the same mesh and material. Enable project build conversion, then use Unity Build or Build And Run as usual.</p><p >• Preview the current scene or project prefab folders, with exclusion reasons.</p><p >• Batch compatible rendering through native GPU instancing while retaining GameObjects, scripts and physics.</p><p >• Use optional Forge Object/Spawner adapters for Burst/ECS movement, rotation, spawning and lifetime.</p><p >• Review dated build history and matching measured performance evidence, and explore three editable samples.</p><p >Conversion applies to player builds. Arbitrary MonoBehaviour code is not translated. Gains depend on CPU/GPU workload; installation alone does not guarantee faster frames.</p><p >Promotional music: Cipher — Kevin MacLeod (incompetech.com). CC BY 3.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/ . Source: https://incompetech.com/music/royalty-free/index.html?isrc=USUAN1100844 . Excerpted, loudness adjusted and faded. Promotional videos only.</p>",
      "summary": "Optimize repeated Unity meshes at build time, preview scene and prefab eligibility, and keep your GameObject workflow. Includes DOTS behavior adapters.",
      "technical": "<p >Validated on Windows with Unity 6000.0.83f1 and Built-in rendering. DOTS player conversion requires com.unity.entities 1.3.15. Editor Play retains GameObjects.</p>",
